jobs.description:
Hands-on work, teamwork, and food production. Become a production worker in the food sector in Horst. Stable job, modern working environment, and plenty of growth opportunities!
Bij welk bedrijf ga je aan de slag als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work at an international family-owned company specializing in the processing and packaging of fresh food products. From a modern and temperature-controlled working environment in Horst, the team works daily on quality, efficiency, and collaboration.
Wat ga je doen als Production WorkerAs a Food Production Worker in Horst, you will work in a dynamic production environment where you are responsible for sorting, processing, and packaging food products according to set guidelines. Together with your colleagues on the production line, you ensure a smooth, efficient, and hygienic production process. You monitor product quality, identify any deviations, and actively contribute to optimizing the process.

You will work in rotating shifts: an early shift from Monday to Saturday, starting at 6:00 AM and typically finishing at 2:00 PM, with possible extension until 3:30 PM. In addition, there is a (late) day shift from Monday to Friday, starting at 12:00 PM and continuing until production is completed. During busier periods, the start time may shift to 2:00 PM.
Wat wij vragen
- Good communication skills and you speak English (Dutch or Polish is a plus);

- You are stress-resistant, enjoy working in a team, and can switch tasks quickly;

- You have no objection to working in a refrigerated environment;

- You are willing to work overtime during peak season;

- You are flexible with working hours (including working every other Saturday).

Wat wij bieden 
- Starting salary of €2,549.73 gross per month, with plenty of growth opportunities based on performance;

- A solid pension scheme as a Food Production Worker in Horst;

- Opportunity for a permanent contract with the company upon good performa

For our client in Amsterdam, we are looking for a key account manager (B2B retail) for the German market. Together with your colleagues from the sales team, you will continue to sell a large assortment of cool, practical, and sustainable products. In this position, you are responsible for expanding the customer base and maintaining the current relationships. Your base location will be our NL office; they prefer that you visit your customers in Germany as much as possible to strengthen the relationship and introduce the newest items. The ratio of new client acquisition to existing client management is 50/50.
Responsibilities: - Develop and maintain strong relationships with key accounts in Germany;
- Identify new business opportunities and drive sales growth;
- Negotiate contracts and agreements with clients;
- Provide excellent customer service and support.
- Collaborate with internal teams to meet customer needs;
- Prepare and deliver sales presentations to potential clients;
- Monitor market trends and competitor activities;
- Meet sales targets and objectives;
- Travel within Germany for client meetings and business development.

RequirementsYou know how to find commercial opportunities, and with your strong drive plus a good dose of perseverance and guts, you grab them. Besides:- Commercially driven;
- Positive, enthusiastic, and friendly;
- Experience in sales or account management for a minimum of 7 years and having worked with key accounts for several years; 
- Business fluent in German (C2 level) and English;
- Familiarity with the German retail / FMCG market and consumer trends is a MUST;
- excellent verbal and written communication abilities;
- Strong problem-solving skills and a proven track record of building and maintaining client relationships
- Living near the Amsterdam area (or have plans to relocate there very soon)

Benefits- 13th month bonus
- 8% holiday allowance
- A full-time (40 hour) contract; first contract is for 7 months.
- Fully onsite

We’re looking for a reach truck operator who is skilled at driving this type of equipment for a dynamic organization in the Echt region. In this role, you’ll be responsible for handling incoming and outgoing goods using a reach truck. Does working in a clean, well-organized facility energize you? This permanent position offers you job security on the day shift!

Duties:

- Placing pallets of products on shelves using a single-deep or double-deep reach truck;
- Picking orders; 
- Assisting with loading containers; 
- Supporting all logistical tasks as they arise.

You’ll spend most of your time operating the reach truck, so it’s important that you have experience with this type of logistics vehicle. Do you see yourself in this role? Don’t hesitate—read on!

This is a day shift position from 6:00 AM to 3:00 PM, Monday through Friday. 

- Experience operating a reach truck and a certificate demonstrating that you possess the qualities of a good reach truck operator;
- You speak Dutch, English, or German.
